From 7ae2240936bcbc6f5469703e16185699905fe10e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 18:37:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 470/572] fix(st-drivers): guard MCE PM context calls
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The MCE driver references saved PM context helpers when restoring
encryption regions, but those helpers are only available when
STM32MP_SUPPORT_PM is enabled.

Guard the reload and save paths so STM32MP13 builds without PM support
do not compile references to the context helpers.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 010455aeff929a992faee4e7b707cbb5ad05b276 fix(st-drivers): guard MCE PM context calls]
Change-Id: Iab2bd91d661a88119c22146328711365ec6d1cb7
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/st/mce/stm32_mce.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/st/mce/stm32_mce.c b/drivers/st/mce/stm32_mce.c
index ec2fa292e9..63318bb79f 100644
--- a/drivers/st/mce/stm32_mce.c
+++ b/drivers/st/mce/stm32_mce.c
@@ -349,6 +349,7 @@ int stm32_mce_get_address_encryption_state(uint32_t address, uint32_t *state)
 
 void stm32_mce_reload_configuration(void)
 {
+#if STM32MP_SUPPORT_PM
 	uint32_t idx;
 
 	for (idx = 0U; idx < MCE_IP_MAX_REGION_NB; idx++) {
@@ -367,6 +368,7 @@ void stm32_mce_reload_configuration(void)
 			panic();
 		}
 	}
+#endif
 }
 
 static int fconf_populate_mce(uintptr_t config)
@@ -416,7 +418,9 @@ static int fconf_populate_mce(uintptr_t config)
 			panic();
 		}
 
+#if STM32MP_SUPPORT_PM
 		stm32mp1_pm_save_mce_region(i, &region);
+#endif
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-- 
2.53.0

